# Trivy baseline for eg-esign — reviewed 2026-07-27.
#
# The dependency scan (jenkins/security-scan.groovy) blocks on fixable
# HIGH/CRITICAL findings. Everything listed here was triaged and could NOT be
# resolved by a trivial version bump. Anything NOT listed here still fails the
# build, so a newly-introduced vulnerability is caught.
#
# Fixed rather than ignored in this same change (16 -> 5 findings):
#   axios 1.16.0 -> ^1.18.0                    (override)
#   fast-uri 3.1.2 -> ^3.1.4                   (override)
#   brace-expansion 1.1.12/5.0.7 -> ^5.0.8     (override)
#   @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger -> ^2.9.0 (override)
#   next 16.2.6 -> 16.2.11                     (apps/docs, apps/openpage-api)
#   sharp 0.34.5 -> ^0.35.0                    (packages/lib + override)
#
# Scope note: this file applies to the *filesystem* scan of the source tree.
# Verified against the built image on 2026-07-27 — react-router, sharp and
# brace-expansion ARE present in the runtime image, so these are real (if
# low-reachability) exposures, not purely dev-tree noise. They are baselined
# because no trivial fix exists, not because they are absent.
#
# Re-triage when the nightly upstream-sync bumps these dependencies.

# react-router 7.18.1 -> 8.3.0
# Not a trivial bump: react-router IS the application framework (apps/remix
# runs React Router v7 in framework mode). A 7 -> 8 major upgrade is its own
# project with route-module and typegen changes, not a CI-unblocking patch.
# Reached here only as a transitive dep of fumadocs-core in apps/docs, which
# does not ship.
GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2

# postcss 8.4.31 -> 8.5.12 / 8.5.18
# Nested inside `next` (apps/docs, apps/openpage-api) as
# node_modules/next/node_modules/postcss. The root postcss is already 8.5.19
# and the repo's existing `overrides.postcss: ^8.5.19` does not reach a
# workspace-nested copy. Neither app is built into the container.
CVE-2026-45623
GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849

# brace-expansion 2.1.2 -> 5.0.8
# The root copy is overridden to 5.0.8; three packages keep a nested 2.x that
# npm `overrides` does not rewrite:
#   @hono/vite-dev-server (dev server), filelist (jake), google-gax (grpc codegen)
CVE-2026-14257

# sharp 0.34.5 -> 0.35.0
# packages/lib now declares 0.35.0 and there is an `overrides.sharp: ^0.35.0`,
# but a 0.34.5 copy stays hoisted at node_modules/sharp: it arrives as an
# optional dependency of `next`, and npm does not apply `overrides` to
# optional deps resolved that way. `npm ls sharp` reports it as "invalid".
# Removing it needs next's own sharp bump, not something this repo controls.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
